export const SPEC = "# MyArcade game development specification (spec 1)\n\n**Owner's responsibility.** Publishing a game is the owner's own decision and risk. MyArcade asks the owner to accept that responsibility before each publish; 2nfro and the makers of Bot Gateway do not check games.\n\n## 1. Rules that come first\n\n1. **Make an original game.** Do not recreate or imitate an existing game: not its name, characters, art, music, levels or overall look, and not a renamed copy. A genre or a general mechanic is fine; if the request describes a specific existing game, say so and propose an original design instead.\n2. **Everything is inside the pack.** No CDN, no web fonts, no analytics, no outside address of any kind. The site's security policy blocks them, so the game would break.\n3. **Bundle to one JavaScript file.** Libraries are bundled in.\n\n## 2. What to deliver\n\nA folder (the *game pack*) with flat file names, no sub-folders:\n\n```text\nmygame/\n  game.json    description (section 3)\n  game.js      one ES module, the game (section 4)\n  cover.svg    the lobby card's picture, viewBox 0 0 88 112 (or .png / .webp)\n  ...          optional assets (section 5)\n```\n\nLimits:\n\n| Item | Limit |\n|---|---|\n| Files in a pack | 20 |\n| One file | 4 MB |\n| File names | letters, digits, `-`, `_`, `.`; not starting with `.` |\n| File types | `js json svg png jpg jpeg webp gif mp3 ogg wav m4a woff2 bin` |\n\nKeep it small: every byte goes through the owner's home connection and is not compressed. Aim for under 1 MB in total.\n\n## 3. game.json\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spec\": 1,\n  \"id\": \"comet-run\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"kind\": \"2d\",\n  \"engine\": \"canvas\",\n  \"entry\": \"game.js\",\n  \"cover\": \"cover.svg\",\n  \"stage\": \"wide\",\n  \"tags\": [\"action\", \"solo\"],\n  \"text\": {\n    \"en\": {\n      \"title\": \"Comet Run\",\n      \"blurb\": \"One or two sentences for the lobby card.\",\n      \"howto\": \"Arrows move · Space boost · P pause\"\n    },\n    \"zh-TW\": { \"title\": \"彗星快跑\", \"blurb\": \"大廳卡片的簡介。\", \"howto\": \"方向鍵移動 · 空白鍵加速 · P 暫停\" }\n  },\n  \"panel\": [\n    \"score\",\n    { \"key\": \"fuel\", \"label\": { \"en\": \"Fuel\", \"zh-TW\": \"燃料\" } },\n    \"level\"\n  ],\n  \"pad\": [\n    { \"action\": \"left\", \"label\": \"left\" },\n    { \"action\": \"right\", \"label\": \"right\" },\n    { \"action\": \"boost\", \"label\": { \"en\": \"Boost\", \"zh-TW\": \"加速\" } }\n  ],\n  \"max_score\": 1000000\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `spec` | `1` |\n| `id` | lower-case letters, digits, `-`; 2 to 32 characters |\n| `version` | `major.minor.patch`; a new pack of the same game needs a new version |\n| `kind` | `2d` or `3d` |\n| `engine` | `canvas`, `three`, `phaser` or `other` (information only) |\n| `entry` | `game.js` |\n| `cover` | a file in the pack |\n| `stage` | `wide` (landscape, up to 960 px wide) or `standard` (portrait, 1:2) |\n| `tags` | any of `action puzzle platform classic solo`; others are shown as written |\n| `text` | `en` is required with `title`, `blurb`, `howto`; also possible: `zh-TW`, `zh-CN`, `ja`, `es` |\n| `panel` | side panel rows: `\"score\"`, `\"level\"`, or `{key, label}` matching `stats` in section 4 |\n| `pad` | on-screen buttons for touch screens. `action` is passed to `input()`. `label` is a shell word (`left right up down jump`) or a language map |\n| `max_score` | optional; higher scores are refused by the server |\n\n## 4. game.js: the contract\n\nThe shell (not the game) draws the room: title bar, frame, Start / Pause / Game over overlay, side panel, how-to line, touch buttons, mute. The game draws **only into the canvas it is given**.\n\n```js\nexport function mount(canvas, host) {\n  // set up, draw the first frame, then:\n  host.update({ status: \"ready\", score: 0, level: 1 });\n\n  return {\n    start() {},                 // begin a new run (also from \"over\")\n    pause() {},\n    resume() {},\n    input(action, down) {},     // a pad button; down = true / false\n    destroy() {},               // remove EVERYTHING (below)\n  };\n}\n```\n\n`host`, given by the shell:\n\n| Member | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `host.update(state)` | Call on every change. `state`: `status` (required: `ready`, `playing`, `paused`, `over`), `score` (integer), `level` (integer), `won` (boolean, for `over`), `stats` (object for the panel, for example `{ fuel: 3 }`) |\n| `host.isMuted()` | Check before every sound; it can change at any time |\n| `host.lang` | `en`, `zh-TW`, `zh-CN`, `ja` or `es` |\n| `host.assetUrl(name)` | The address of a file in the pack. Never build an address yourself |\n\nThe shell counts a play when `status` goes from `ready` or `over` to `playing`, and records the score when it goes to `over`.\n\nThe game must:\n\n- **Fit the canvas.** Follow its size with a `ResizeObserver`; set `canvas.width` and `canvas.height` (with `devicePixelRatio`, at most 2) but never its CSS size. The shell owns the layout.\n- **Play by keyboard and touch.** Every action has a key and a `pad` button. Call `preventDefault()` on arrows and space. Ignore keys when the target is an `input`, `textarea` or `select`.\n- **Pause.** `P` or `Escape` toggles pause; pause when `document.hidden` becomes true.\n- **Use `Enter` or space** to start from `ready` and `over`.\n- **Have a `destroy()`:** close the `AudioContext` and stop timers. The game runs in its own sandboxed frame, which is thrown away when the player leaves.\n\n## 5. What the browser will refuse\n\nThe game runs in a sandboxed frame with this security policy, which a game cannot change. It has no origin, no network and no storage:\n\n```text\nsandbox allow-scripts; default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline' blob:; style-src 'unsafe-inline';\nimg-src blob: data:; media-src blob: data:; font-src blob: data:; connect-src blob: data:\n```\n\n| Do not use | Use instead |\n|---|---|\n| Inline `<script>`, a single HTML file | `game.js` only; the pack has no HTML |\n| `import` of a package or an address, `import()` | Bundle everything into one file |\n| `eval`, `new Function`, string `setTimeout` | Ordinary functions |\n| WebAssembly (Godot, Unity, wasm physics) | Plain JavaScript |\n| `<audio>`, `new Audio()`, `<video>` | Web Audio: oscillators, or `fetch(host.assetUrl(\"x.mp3\"))` + `decodeAudioData` (the check refuses them, though the frame could play blobs) |\n| iframes, new windows, adding elements to the page | Draw in the canvas |\n| Web fonts from outside, CSS `@import` | `woff2` in the pack with `FontFace(name, \"url(\" + host.assetUrl(\"x.woff2\") + \")\")` and `document.fonts.add`; or plain canvas text |\n| `fetch` other than `host.assetUrl` files | Nothing: a game has no server and no network |\n| `localStorage`, cookies, `location`, `document.body` | Keep state in memory; storage belongs to the shell |\n\n`AudioContext` must be created or resumed after a user action (Start is one). Images load with `new Image()` and `host.assetUrl`. WebGL and `three` work in the given canvas.\n\n## 6. Done means\n\n- [ ] Plays from Start to game over and starts again, by keyboard and by touch.\n- [ ] Pause, resume, and leaving the browser tab all pause correctly.\n- [ ] Mute silences every sound at once.\n- [ ] Resizing the window keeps the picture correct.\n- [ ] No console errors.\n- [ ] Every text is in `game.json` or is drawn according to `host.lang`.\n- [ ] Original: nothing copied from an existing game (section 1).";
